{"golden_id": "tg-3efe38f6", "kind": "table_row", "assertion_or_record_ids": ["maudsley-taylor-2021:table:127:0020", "row:0"], "expectation": {"type": "table-row-cells", "title": "Table 1.18 (Continued)", "row_index": 0, "cells": [{"text": "Metformin2,32,53,54\n(500–2000mg/day)", "blank": false}, {"text": "Now a substantial database (in non-diabetic patients) supporting the use of\nmetformin in both reducing and reversing weight gain caused by antipsychotics\n(mainly olanzapine). Beneficial effects on other metabolic parameters. Some negative\nstudies, but clear and significant effect in meta-analyses. One positive RCT55 and\nextension study56 in children and adolescents with ASD published since then. Ideal for\nthose with weight gain and diabetes or polycystic ovary syndrome. Note that\nmetformin treatment increases the risk of vitamin B12 deficiency57", "blank": false}]}, "verified": true, "verified_by": "independent-recompute", "notes": "deterministic fill"}
